 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "The Leaning Tower of Pisa started leaning before it was even finished.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Under it is soft clay and sand, and one side is softer than the other.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then a war stopped the building for almost a hundred years. That pause saved it.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The clay had time to squeeze out its water and get stronger before more floors went up.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But it kept tilting, a little every year, until it was over five degrees.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "In 1990 it was closed. Engineers first stacked lead weights on the high side.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then they did something weird: they slowly pulled soil out from under the high side.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The high side settled down, and the tower straightened by about forty five centimeters.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "It still leans, on purpose, and it should stay that way for centuries. Now you know.",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
